# Chunked C emission (plans/CHUNKED_C_EMISSION.md steps 2-3): `--emit-chunks N`
# splits the emitted program into N linkable translation units, compiles them in
# parallel behind a content-addressed `.o` cache, and links. The case runs the
# SAME compile twice, so the golden pins both halves of the cache contract: the
# first run compiles every unit, the second serves all of them from cache.
#
# stdout_keep: the only deterministic lines are the allocator notice and the
# per-run chunk summary. Everything else (paths, timings) varies by sandbox.
#
# The `ignore` file drops the generated artifacts: object files and the linked
# binary are not reproducible across clang versions, and the emitted C/header
# would force a golden re-record on every codegen change — the assertion here is
# the CACHE BEHAVIOUR and a successful link, not the bytes of the output.
stdout_keep=^(chunks: |Using )
timeout=300
